      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T07:15:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find this approach somewhat questionable, TBH. It feels very \"I\u0027m gonna solve this very specific problem that happened this one time\", and thus doesn\u0027t feel like it belongs in a build system.\n\nWhat other approaches were considered before you decided on this one? Is there any way we could make this solution more general-purpose? One approach that comes to mind to me would be something like:\n\n```\nstatic_library(\"foo\") {\n    tool(\"alink\") {\n       ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nTo just allow overriding of the tool\n\nAlternatively, perhaps we could simply come up with a way to use the link args elsewhere.\n\nKeep in mind that I\u0027m not strictly saying we shouldn\u0027t be doing this, just that I\u0027m very hesitant about adding something to a build system that isn\u0027t general-purpose.",
      "revId": "e84b7b7fceac46ffbaefbd3ed3a31a6dc27e5249",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46deec7a_e171fb7f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T08:14:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with your concern. I asked whether we can expect llvm to have the previous behavior where we don\u0027t need wrapper in https://crbug.com/542981236#comment14\n\nGemini proposed some other solutions like\n1. extend `generated_file` to support linker inputs collection\n1. support copying response file from other target\n\nBut I feel this solution is simpler and have some similarity with `write_runtime_deps`. So I asked Gemini to implement this feature.\n\nIt is bit hard to decide which of extensibility or simplicity is important here, but if we don\u0027t have ohter use case of extensibility, I prefer to have simpler interface for now.",
      "parentUuid": "ee07004a_6f9228bf",
      "revId": "e84b7b7fceac46ffbaefbd3ed3a31a6dc27e5249",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
